---
lawsID: "dflt-law-001"
name: "Default Universal Law (6-Step)"
version: 1.0
author: "System Designer"
universeID: "Synex"
inheritsFrom: "universal-hermetic-000"
tags: ["law", "default", "6-step", "0.5-baseline"]
abstract: "Provides default universal constraints and synergy guidelines for the six-step architecture, ensuring cycic equilibrium near 0.5."

dynamic_attributes:
  synergy_measure:
    name: "E_total"
    default_baseline: 0.5
    description: "Tracks total synergy across all steps; tries to remain near 0.5 or any seeded midpoint."
  
  cycic_threshold:
    name: "epsilon_cyclic"
    default_value: 0.03
    description: "If |E_total - 0.5| < 0.03, synergy is considered stable. Otherwise, partial resets or expansions apply."

  # Optional: Additional universal attributes
  polarity:
    axis: "Harmonic-Disharmonic"
    default_state: "Harmonic"
    fluctuation_range: "-0.5 to 0.5"
  vibration:
    default_intensity: "Medium"
    cycic_sensitivity: 0.1
    description: "How quickly the system reacts to synergy drift."

seed: 0.5  # Typically references default synergy
use_unified_seed: true

## Universal Principles
principles:
  - name: "Dynamic Reciprocity"
    description: "All expansions reflect back to seeds, forming cycic synergy."
    effect: "Mandates a feedback loop at each step: Potential to Recursion, then re-check seeds."
  - name: "Fractal Correspondence"
    description: "Micro changes at one step mirror macro changes across the six-step flow."
    effect: "A small offset in Step 1 can ripple to Step 6, then feed back and unify synergy measure."

## Update and Enforcement Policies
update_policies:
  - frequency: "Event-Driven"  # The law updates whenever synergy drifts outside cycic threshold
  - approval_process: "Consensus or Automated"  # E.g., partial expansions if drift is mild

## Related Items
related_items:
  - type: "aligned with"
    target: "dflt-dyn-001"
    description: "References the default dynamic attributes for the 6-step approach."

## Universal_Principles (Optional Extended)
universal_principles:
  - name: "Seed-Centric"
    description: "Seeds (baseline ~ 0.5) unify expansions across steps."
    effect: "Ensures no step or domain overshadow synergy’s balanced midpoint."
  - name: "Cycic Re-centering"
    description: "If synergy measure drifts, partial resets or advanced expansions re-align."
    effect: "Maintains E_total ≈ 0.5 ± epsilon_cyclic."

file_variation_rules:
  - fileType: ".tune"
    variations:
      - principle: "Cycic Re-centering"
        allowable_range: "-0.5 to +0.5 from baseline"
        example_effects: "If synergy overshoots, logistic or exponential re-centering triggers."

description: |
  The “Default Universal Law (6-Step)” file enforces cycic harmony for the Potential→Symmetry→Flow→Connectivity→Emergence→Recursion loop.
  It references a synergy measure near 0.5, employing partial expansions or resets if drift from the cycic threshold is detected. This law
  ensures each step remains in fractal correspondence with others and seeds unify expansions.

attachments: []
...
